0.22.13

### 0.22.13
- 2026-05-17: updater now looks for `scripts/install.py` (current layout) with fallback to `install.py` at the tarball root for older releases.

### 0.22.12
- 2026-05-17: README runtime-deps list now includes watchdog and pathspec.

### 0.22.11
- 2026-05-17: tests workflow now also triggers on push to master + workflow_dispatch so the status badge actually populates.

### 0.22.10
- 2026-05-17: commit_worker shows a "working" task at start so the gesture registers immediately even when the pre-stage pull is slow.
- 2026-05-17: kick_off_workers supervisor releases refresh locks in a finally so a raising refresh_repo can't strand a repo in refreshing state.

### 0.22.9
- 2026-05-17: test bootstrap also writes user.name/email to the temp gitconfig so CI integration tests don't hit "Please tell me who you are" on merge/propagate commits.

### 0.22.8
- 2026-05-17: tests/_helpers.py bootstraps a throwaway GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL with protocol.file.allow=always so idlegit's git() can use file:// remotes on git 2.38+.

### 0.22.7
- 2026-05-17: pull-all summary now reports `up-to-date` correctly (was always 0 because `_pull_prefer_ff_then_merge` returns True for both moved and already-up-to-date) — track HEAD before/after the pull per repo to distinguish.
- 2026-05-17: smart-sync's final-refresh parallel map is now exception-safe — a failing `refresh_repo` no longer escapes the `finally` and leaves spinners stuck + the header task in "running".
- 2026-05-17: help pages updated — review-screen page (06) added covering then-runs and Ctrl+K; configuration page documents `fetch_on_manual_refresh` and `auto_recurse_submodules`; keyboard-shortcuts page documents Ctrl+K and the full review-pane gesture set; getting-started page no longer says "idlegit does not poll the filesystem" (it does, via watchdog, since 0.19.0).

### 0.22.6
- 2026-05-17: then-run-after-push state (tag / workflow dispatch / `track_workflow` opt-ins) now clears at the moment review is accepted instead of inside `commit_worker` post-push.
- 2026-05-17: New Ctrl+K gesture on the review screen wipes every Repo's then-run state.

### 0.22.5
- 2026-05-17: fix release pipeline — `core/config.py`'s `from .models import …` moved behind a `TYPE_CHECKING` guard + lazy local import inside `load_workspaces`, so setuptools' `version = { attr = "core.config.VERSION" }` directive can `exec_module` the file standalone at build time. Previously the relative import failed during pip install with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'core'`.

### 0.22.4
- 2026-05-17: "Add tag" from the recent-commit dialog now pushes the tag iff the commit is reachable from any `origin/*` ref.

### 0.22.3
- 2026-05-17: updated hint texts

### 0.22.2
- 2026-05-17: pull-all (Ctrl+P) now adds a parent "pull all" task with `n pulled / n up-to-date / n no upstream / n locked / n failed` summary so the gesture is visible even when every repo silently no-ops; smart-sync icon-state lag fixed — final refresh + link_siblings now runs BEFORE the `refreshing` flags clear and the header task is marked terminal.

### 0.22.1
- 2026-05-17: Shortened some hint texts

### 0.22.0
- 2026-05-17: Ctrl+P — workspace-level `pull --ff-only` against every repo with an upstream; honours `auto_recurse_submodules`, runs up to MAX_PARALLEL_GIT_JOBS in parallel, surfaces per-repo task rows. No-upstream repos are silently skipped; non-FF pulls fail (use the action menu's Pull for a merge fallback)

### 0.21.2
- 2026-05-17: fix submodule-parent propagation regression — `_propagate_submodule_bump` now waits up to 5s for the parent's refresh lock instead of silently skipping on contention (fs_watcher could grab the lock in the brief window between push completion and sibling-sync start, leaving the parent's gitlink unbumped)

### 0.21.1
- 2026-05-17: main-screen "edit msg" (Shift+→) hint now shows whenever the focused row is commit-able, not just when a message has been typed

### 0.21.0
- 2026-05-17: `auto_recurse_submodules` (default on) makes idlegit's pull/fetch pass `--recurse-submodules=on-demand`; `fetch_on_manual_refresh` (default off) makes Ctrl+R fetch from origin per repo before re-reading state so ahead/behind reflects upstream. Both are workspace-overridable and surface as toggle rows in the workspace settings modal's SMART-SYNC section.

### 0.20.3
- 2026-05-17: fs-watcher gate-order fix — `on_event` / `_on_timer` now check `tasks.has_running()` before `repo.refreshing` so user edits during a commit pipeline route to the post-task drain queue instead of being dropped; `release_refresh` no longer clears the spinner flag when the underlying lock was already unlocked; `fire_refresh` bails when the watcher was torn down mid-drain

### 0.20.2
- 2026-05-17: per-repo refresh mutex — every refresh source (fs_watcher, Ctrl+R, action menu, commit pipeline) now claims `Repo.refresh_lock` non-blocking and bails when another source already holds it, eliminating cross-source races on the row's status fields

### 0.20.1
- 2026-05-17: help page added for auto-refresh (toggle, debounce, per-workspace gitignore-style ignore list); shortcuts + configuration pages cross-link to it

### 0.20.0
- 2026-05-17: per-workspace `fs_watch_ignore` (gitignore-style patterns) editable in the workspace settings modal; auto-refresh now uses a single persistent debounce thread per repo (was spawning a thread per event under bursts — could exhaust per-process thread limits) and suspends entirely while any action/task is running, draining one refresh per affected repo on the has-running → idle transition

### 0.19.2
